  "dis": "CWT-MB328B(II) Modbus I/O module, 8 digital inputs and 18 relay outputs",
  "status": "datasheet only",
  "protocols": [
    "modbus_rtu",
    "modbus_tcp"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unitId": 1,
    "baudrate": 9600,
    "parity": "N",
    "dataBits": 8,
    "stopBits": 1,
    "tcpHost": "192.168.1.1",
    "tcpPort": 502,
    "blockSize": 32
  },
  "notes": [
    "Every unit ships as slave ID 1, and every -SE as 192.168.1.1: give each unit a unique ID or address before it joins a bus or network.",
    "Inputs are wet (5 to 30 VDC). A dry contact needs a supply wired through it. Not for mains voltage.",
    "Relays are rated 5 A resistive: switch motors, compressors and large lights through contactors.",
    "What the relays do on loss of communications and at power-up is not documented. Do not use them where a stuck-on relay is unsafe until this is tested on the bench.",
    "The manual uses 1-based addresses (00001, 10001); the template stores the 0-based wire address and shows the manual address."
  ],
